I never said arbitrary was bad. It just means that, no matter what,
there will be at least one dissenter. Personally, I'm not too bothered
what the days are called, as long as they're called something.

 

________________________________

From: lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com
[mailto:lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com] On Behalf Of Luke Bergen
Sent: 26 January 2011 15:30
To: lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com
Subject: Re: [lojban-beginners] days of the week

 

Arbitrary is not necessarily bad.  Sometimes there is no logical,
rational reason for doing something a particular way.  I had 2 pairs of
socks this morning which were identical in every way.  One pair was on
the left side of my drawer, the other was on the right.  I picked the
left pair.  Was it an arbitrary choice?  Yes.  Did I spend 80 emails
going back and forth with my wife trying to come up with a more
"rational" reason for choosing the left or the right pair?  ummm, no.

 

"But are you right or left handed?" say the jbodau.  Screw it!  I just
want my damn socks.

On Wed, Jan 26, 2011 at 10:07 AM, Alex Rozenshteyn
<rpglover64@gmail.com> wrote:



And therein lies our problem.

 

On Wed, Jan 26, 2011 at 9:45 AM, Michael Eaton
<michael.eaton@blackpool.gov.uk> wrote:



Whatever system or derivation is used, it will always be arbitrary.

 

________________________________

From: lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com
[mailto:lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com] On Behalf Of Oren
Sent: 26 January 2011 14:26


To: lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com
Subject: Re: [lojban-beginners] days of the week

 

As an avid admirer of logic in Mandarin Chinese, my initial position was
that numbered days are just more logical, more straightforward, etc.

 

But wow! Using colors makes way more sense if it's something that
naturally cycles in sevens... otherwise, it's still totally arbitrary
(okay, i mean "practical") to choose a seven-day cycle.

 

On Wed, Jan 26, 2011 at 09:06, Michael Eaton
<michael.eaton@blackpool.gov.uk> wrote:




Agreed. The counter-argument, of course, being "starting the cycles from
a moving point might not be acceptable to other cultures".

 

Just one of those things.

 

________________________________

From: lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com
[mailto:lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com] On Behalf Of Luke Bergen
Sent: 26 January 2011 14:04


To: lojban-beginners@googlegroups.com
Subject: Re: [lojban-beginners] days of the week

 

Being completely honest and serious for a moment... your idea was my
favorite gejyspa.  I'm not sure why people didn't take it seriously.  I
think one of the complaints was "but it's still starting the cycles at a
constant spot so it might not be acceptable for some cultures" to which
I say "well, it has to start somewhere and yes, sometimes learning a
foreign language is difficult".

 

 

